WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.750
Step 1: Select the employee’s employer location. Open their Pay Conditions in Users, or Award compliance → Employee details → Edit details.

2
00:00:07.750 --> 00:00:18.000
Step 2: Choose Add Individual Flexibility Agreement (IFA). Record the retained signed agreement reference, signing date, start date and any end date. The employer comes from this location’s Employer setup.

3
00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:30.125
Step 3: Select the terms the signed agreement varies. If it permits rostered hours instead of fixed regular hours, select When work is performed and confirm that specific permission. Record what changes and the better-off-overall assessment.

4
00:00:30.125 --> 00:00:43.208
Step 4: Confirm the required signatures, including a parent or guardian for an employee under 18, and that the original is retained and the employee received a copy. Press Save employment details. Choosing or previewing fields does not save.

5
00:00:43.208 --> 00:00:57.208
Step 5: A current working-hours-only IFA allows part-time costs without fixed regular hours at that employer location. Actual hours use the published roster; time outside it attracts overtime. Standard award limits and pay rules remain. Other varied pay terms require separate review.
